## Summary

Your first spec, written by `quickstart.py`. It describes a tiny script so you can see the shape before you write a real one. A spec says WHAT must be true, the plan says HOW and in which steps, and a reviewer that did not write the code gives the verdict. Edit it, or delete this folder and ask your assistant to write the next one with the `sdd-feature` skill.

Check it any time with:

```
python3 ~/.claude/scripts/spec_lint.py {{SPEC_DIR}}
```

## Glossary

Every acceptance criterion names one of these as its subject.

- **Greeter**: the script `hello.py`.

## User Stories

- As a newcomer, I want a script that greets me by name, so that I can see a spec turn into code.

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] AC-01: WHEN the user passes a name, THE Greeter SHALL print `Hello, <name>!` on one line.
- [ ] AC-02: IF no name is passed, THEN THE Greeter SHALL print `Hello, world!` and exit 0.

